    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34146" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμμεν-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>abiding in</i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἐ</span>. <i>steadfastness</i>, Timo<i><span class="en">
				58.1
			</span></i> (s.v.l.).—<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> has only neut. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμμενές</span> as
				Adv., always in phrase, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ.
				αἰεί</span>
			<i>unceasing</i> ever, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.361
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.386
			</span></i>, etc. (without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰεί</span> in
			later 
				Ep.
			, as <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				83
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἤματα πάντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					339
				</span></i>
			): also Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νέως, ἐμάχοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					712
				</span></i>
			.</div>
